 creates objects through a method; Singleton limits a class to one"],["text","instance; Builder constructs complex objects step by step."],["text","Structural: Adapter converts an interface; Decorator wraps an object to add behavior; Facade"],["text","simplifies subsystem access."],["text","Behavioral: Strategy swaps algorithms; Observer notifies subscribers; Command represents a"],["text","request as an object."],["text","Interview question: What is the Strategy pattern?"],["text","Answer: It encapsulates interchangeable algorithms behind a common interface."],["text","Remember: Client → Strategy interface → interchangeable implementations"]]